From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:26:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] package/tensorflow-lite: align GPU delegate image pitch
 in pixels

With Mesa 25.2, RustiCL on freedreno a6xx offers
cl_khr_image2d_from_buffer with a pitch alignment of 64 pixels, and
the TensorFlow Lite GPU delegate switches to images on shared
buffers. On Adreno it divides the reported alignment by the bytes per
pixel (Qualcomm's driver reports bytes), so every such image gets a
pitch RustiCL rejects and the delegate fails on the Adreno 623 and
702 alike:

  TfLiteGpuDelegate Init: Failed to create Image2D from Buffer
  (clCreateImage): Invalid image descriptor

Add a patch that aligns to the reported value in pixels, as the
OpenCL specification defines it; that pitch satisfies a driver that
means bytes too.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 ...ates-gpu-align-image-pitch-in-pixels.patch | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/tensorflow-lite/0007-lite-delegates-gpu-align-image-pitch-in-pixels.patch

diff --git a/package/tensorflow-lite/0007-lite-delegates-gpu-align-image-pitch-in-pixels.patch b/package/tensorflow-lite/0007-lite-delegates-gpu-align-image-pitch-in-pixels.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..6622d84073
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/tensorflow-lite/0007-lite-delegates-gpu-align-image-pitch-in-pixels.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
+Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0400
+Subject: [PATCH] lite/delegates/gpu: align image pitch in pixels
+
+CL_DEVICE_IMAGE_PITCH_ALIGNMENT is in pixels, but on Adreno the
+delegate divides it by the bytes per pixel, as Qualcomm's driver
+reports it in bytes. Mesa RustiCL reports pixels (64 on freedreno
+a6xx since Mesa 25.2), so the pitch of every image created from a
+shared buffer is too small and clCreateImage fails:
+
+  TfLiteGpuDelegate Init: Failed to create Image2D from Buffer
+  (clCreateImage): Invalid image descriptor
+
+Align to the reported value in pixels: a driver that means bytes is
+satisfied by that pitch too.
+
+Upstream: N/A, TensorFlow 2.11; the code is unchanged in TensorFlow
+master
+
+Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
+---
+--- a/tensorflow/lite/delegates/gpu/cl/inference_context.cc
++++ b/tensorflow/lite/delegates/gpu/cl/inference_context.cc
+@@ -173,9 +173,8 @@
+       const size_t width = shape.b * shape.w;
+       const size_t height = shape.h * DivideRoundUp(shape.c, 4);
+       size_t width_pixel_alignment = gpu_info.opencl_info.image_pitch_alignment;
+-      if (gpu_info.IsAdreno() && width_pixel_alignment % bytes_per_pixel == 0) {
+-        width_pixel_alignment /= bytes_per_pixel;
+-      }
++      // CL_DEVICE_IMAGE_PITCH_ALIGNMENT is in pixels. Aligning to that many
++      // pixels also satisfies a driver that reports it in bytes.
+       const size_t width_aligned = AlignByN(width, width_pixel_alignment);
+       buffer_size = width_aligned * bytes_per_pixel * height;
+     } else {
+@@ -581,10 +580,8 @@
+                  : tensor_desc.GetBHWCShape().c);
+         size_t width_pixel_alignment =
+             gpu_info.opencl_info.image_pitch_alignment;
+-        if (gpu_info.IsAdreno() &&
+-            width_pixel_alignment % bytes_per_pixel == 0) {
+-          width_pixel_alignment /= bytes_per_pixel;
+-        }
++        // CL_DEVICE_IMAGE_PITCH_ALIGNMENT is in pixels. Aligning to that many
++        // pixels also satisfies a driver that reports it in bytes.
+         RETURN_IF_ERROR(CreateTensorSharedImage2DBuffer(
+             *context, shared_buffers_[buffer_index].GetMemoryPtr(), tensor_desc,
+             width_pixel_alignment, &shared_buffer_tensors_[tensor_index]));
+-- 
